    "body": "**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\r\nGNL are making changes to how the Cookie Banner works in the EU/EEA (but not UK) - we need to make some changes as well.\r\n\r\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\r\nCurrently, we display the cookie banner if the ckns_explicit cookie's value is not `1` (ie it is `0` or not set)\r\n\r\nWe now need to consider a value of 2 as also reflecting acceptance of the cookie banner.\r\n\r\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n**Implementation detail:**\r\nWe currently have [this function](https://github.com/bbc/simorgh/blob/latest/src/app/containers/ConsentBanner/CanonicalLogic/index.js#L30)\r\n```js\r\nconst showCookieBanner = () =>\r\n  Cookie.get(EXPLICIT_COOKIE) !== COOKIE_BANNER_APPROVED;\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis may need to change to\r\n```js\r\nconst EXPLICIT_COOKIE_ACCEPTED_VALUES = ['1', '2'];\r\n\r\nconst showCookieBanner = () =>\r\n  !EXPLICIT_COOKIE_ACCEPTED_VALUES.includes(Cookie.get(EXPLICIT_COOKIE));\r\n```\r\n\r\ni.e. if `EXPLICIT_COOKIE` (ckns_explicit) isnt `1` or `2`, show the banner\r\n\r\n**Testing notes**\r\n[Tester to complete]\r\n\r\nDev insight: Alllllllllll the unit tests\r\n\r\n- [x] This feature is expected to need manual testing.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nAdd any other context or screenshots about the feature request here.\r\n",
